{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArSYLBfeGegPJv9SDbu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VXDkzWE67dSRDaJjjKPix4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-RT1JOq; python3 - <<'E'\np='lib/new_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      routerConfig: _router,\n\"\"\",\"\"\"      routerConfig: _router,\n      // Session replay captures screenshots of the PostHogWidget's subtree;\n      // without it nothing is recorded. Wrapping via builder keeps it above\n      // the Navigator but inside MaterialApp.\n      builder: (context, child) =>\n          PostHogWidget(child: child ?? const SizedBox.shrink()),\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Ticket #4471 – empty replays on the new UI\n\n**Cause:** posthog_flutter session replay works by screenshotting the widget\ntree under a `PostHogWidget`. `LegacyApp` wraps its `MaterialApp` in\n`PostHogWidget`; `NewApp` (go_router, `MaterialApp.router`) never did. Events and\nscreen tracking still work (they come from `Analytics.init()` and\n`PosthogObserver`), which is why only the recording is missing. Project\nsettings and SDK version are not involved.\n\n**Fix:** `lib/new_app.dart` now wraps the app content in `PostHogWidget` via\n`MaterialApp.router(builder: ...)`, so it sits above the router's Navigator.\n\n**Not verified:** I couldn't run Flutter/PostHog here. Check on a device that a\nnew-UI session shows up in Replay. Past sessions on the new UI are not\nrecoverable. Also note `maskAllTexts = true` is set, so text will appear masked\nin recordings (by design).\nE\ngit diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1647,"cache_read_input_tokens":20747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1647},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2075540d-4f58-47fb-8414-241b15bbc1ff","uuid":"2ea1776b-a9b9-4cd2-91a3-4c10a7dbb6a2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:03:40.099Z","request_id":"req_011CgArSXzqtGQuEogWaQV4c","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VXDkzWE67dSRDaJjjKPix4":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-RT1JOq; python3 - <<'E'\np='lib/new_app.dart'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      routerConfig: _router,\n\"\"\",\"\"\"      routerConfig: _router,\n      // Session replay captures screenshots of the PostHogWidget's subtree;\n      // without it nothing is recorded. Wrapping via builder keeps it above\n      // the Navigator but inside MaterialApp.\n      builder: (context, child) =>\n          PostHogWidget(child: child ?? const SizedBox.shrink()),\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Ticket #4471 – empty replays on the new UI\n\n**Cause:** posthog_flutter session replay works by screenshotting the widget\ntree under a `PostHogWidget`. `LegacyApp` wraps its `MaterialApp` in\n`PostHogWidget`; `NewApp` (go_router, `MaterialApp.router`) never did. Events and\nscreen tracking still work (they come from `Analytics.init()` and\n`PosthogObserver`), which is why only the recording is missing. Project\nsettings and SDK version are not involved.\n\n**Fix:** `lib/new_app.dart` now wraps the app content in `PostHogWidget` via\n`MaterialApp.router(builder: ...)`, so it sits above the router's Navigator.\n\n**Not verified:** I couldn't run Flutter/PostHog here. Check on a device that a\nnew-UI session shows up in Replay. Past sessions on the new UI are not\nrecoverable. Also note `maskAllTexts = true` is set, so text will appear masked\nin recordings (by design).\nE\ngit diff --stat"}}}
